    <node id="G08"><data key="n_name">Pdcd10 (animal model, species not stated)</data><data key="n_bipartite">gene</data><data key="n_entity_type">gene</data><data key="n_species">animal model, species not stated</data><data key="n_ambiguity">Model species not named.</data></node>
    <node id="D01"><data key="n_name">cerebral cavernous malformation (CCM)</data><data key="n_bipartite">disease</data><data key="n_entity_type">disease</data><data key="n_species">human</data><data key="n_ambiguity">&#x27;CCM&#x27; also prefixes gene-set terms (CCM genes, CCM complexes, CCM genotype) and lesion terms (CCM lesions); those mentions are role-tagged, not disease mentions.</data></node>
    <node id="D02"><data key="n_name">familial cerebral cavernous malformation (FCCM)</data><data key="n_bipartite">disease</data><data key="n_entity_type">disease</data><data key="n_species">human</data><data key="n_ambiguity">Includes &#x27;clinical FCCM&#x27; (no mutation detected) and gene-confirmed FCCM, as the paper does.</data></node>
